IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgk-part9-declared`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026):
-- Part 9 (Investigations), ss 237 to 242: who bears the cost of an investigation, the inspector's report as evidence, the inspector's helpers,
-- the suspension of actions and proceedings by a declared company, winding up, and the offences.
-- The party and act types of the regulative rules are in sgk-part9-declared.l4.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. The Minister, the inspectors and the Court appear only as what their acts mean to the person.
-- Winding up has moved to the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018, which is not a source: its outcomes enter as inputs named for the fact.
-- Marks in the comments: "FALSE-kind" and "NOTHING-kind" say why a branch answers JUST FALSE or NOTHING; "fork F-Kn" points at the fork register of NOTES.md.

§ `Section 237: who bears the cost of an investigation`

DECLARE `s 237(1) direction of the Minister` IS ONE OF
    `s 237(1) the Minister has given no direction`
    `s 237(1) the Minister directs that the applicants pay`
    `s 237(1) the Minister directs that the company pay in part and the applicants in part`

DECLARE `s 237(1) who must pay` IS ONE OF
    `s 237(1) the company investigated`
    `s 237(1) the applicants`
    `s 237(1) the company in part and the applicants in part`

-- src:22247 | 237.—(1) The expenses of and incidental to an investigation by an
-- src:22248 | inspector appointed pursuant to sections 232 and 243 (including the
-- src:22249 | costs of any proceedings brought by the Minister in the name of the
-- src:22250 | company), must be paid by the company investigated or if the
-- src:22251 | Minister so directs by the applicants or in part by the company and in
-- src:22252 | part by the applicants.
@ref s 237(1) (src:22247-22252)
GIVEN `the inspector was appointed pursuant to section 232 or section 243` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the direction` IS A `s 237(1) direction of the Minister`
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 237(1) who must pay`
`s 237(1) who must pay the expenses of and incidental to the investigation` MEANS
    IF NOT `the inspector was appointed pursuant to section 232 or section 243`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "an investigation by an inspector appointed pursuant to sections 232 and 243"; the cost of an investigation of a declared company is for section 231(3) and (4) (fork F-K28: "and" is read as "or")
    ELSE CONSIDER `the direction`
         WHEN `s 237(1) the Minister has given no direction` THEN JUST `s 237(1) the company investigated`      -- "must be paid by the company investigated"
         WHEN `s 237(1) the Minister directs that the applicants pay` THEN JUST `s 237(1) the applicants`        -- "or if the Minister so directs by the applicants"
         WHEN `s 237(1) the Minister directs that the company pay in part and the applicants in part` THEN JUST `s 237(1) the company in part and the applicants in part`   -- "or in part by the company and in part by the applicants"

@ref s 237(1) (src:22247-22252)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 231 party` `s 231 act`
`s 237(1) the company investigated must pay the expenses of the investigation` MEANS
    PARTY `s 231 a company` `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 237(1) pay the expenses of and incidental to the investigation`
    WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 231 a company` `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company investigated did not pay the expenses of and incidental to the investigation"

-- (2)(a): "the applicants must make good the deficiency up to the amount by which the security given by them under this Part exceeds the amount (if any) which they have under subsection (1) been directed by the Minister to pay".
-- The deficiency is the sum the company is liable to pay less what it has paid; the ceiling is the security less the amount directed (nothing, if the security does not exceed it).
-- src:22254 | (2) Despite subsection (1) —
-- src:22256 | (a) if the company fails to pay the whole or any part of the sum
-- src:22257 | which it is so liable to pay, the applicants must make good
-- src:22258 | the deficiency up to the amount by which the security
-- src:22259 | given by them under this Part exceeds the amount (if any)
-- src:22260 | which they have under subsection (1) been directed by the
-- src:22261 | Minister to pay; and
-- src:22263 | (b) any balance of the expenses not paid either by the company
-- src:22264 | or the applicants must be paid out of moneys provided by
-- src:22265 | Parliament.
@ref s 237(2) (src:22254-22265)
GIVEN `the sum the company is liable to pay, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the sum the company has paid, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the security given by the applicants under Part 9, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount the Minister has directed the applicants to pay under subsection (1), in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 237(2)(a) the amount the applicants must make good` MEANS
    IF `the sum the company is liable to pay, in Singapore dollars` MINUS `the sum the company has paid, in Singapore dollars` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN (IF `the security given by the applicants under Part 9, in Singapore dollars` MINUS `the amount the Minister has directed the applicants to pay under subsection (1), in Singapore dollars` GREATER THAN 0
          THEN (IF `the sum the company is liable to pay, in Singapore dollars` MINUS `the sum the company has paid, in Singapore dollars` LESS THAN `the security given by the applicants under Part 9, in Singapore dollars` MINUS `the amount the Minister has directed the applicants to pay under subsection (1), in Singapore dollars`
                THEN `the sum the company is liable to pay, in Singapore dollars` MINUS `the sum the company has paid, in Singapore dollars`     -- the whole deficiency, which is within the ceiling
                ELSE `the security given by the applicants under Part 9, in Singapore dollars` MINUS `the amount the Minister has directed the applicants to pay under subsection (1), in Singapore dollars`)   -- "up to the amount by which the security given by them ... exceeds the amount ... directed"
          ELSE 0)     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the security does not exceed the amount directed, so the ceiling is nothing ("up to the amount by which the security ... exceeds")
    ELSE 0            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the company fails to pay the whole or any part of the sum which it is so liable to pay"; the company has not failed (fork F-K5)

@ref s 237(2)(a) (src:22254-22265)
GIVEN `the name of the applicant` IS A STRING
      `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 231 party` `s 231 act`
`s 237(2)(a) the applicants must make good the deficiency` MEANS
    PARTY `s 231 a person` `the name of the applicant`
    MUST `s 237(2)(a) make good the deficiency up to the amount of the security`
    WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 231 a person` `the name of the applicant` BECAUSE "the applicant did not make good the deficiency in the sum the company was liable to pay, up to the amount of the security"

-- src:22263 | (b) any balance of the expenses not paid either by the company
-- src:22264 | or the applicants must be paid out of moneys provided by
-- src:22265 | Parliament.
@ref s 237(2)(b) (src:22263-22265)
GIVEN `the expenses of and incidental to the investigation, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the sum paid by the company, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the sum paid by the applicants, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 237(2)(b) the balance paid out of moneys provided by Parliament` MEANS
    IF `the expenses of and incidental to the investigation, in Singapore dollars` MINUS `the sum paid by the company, in Singapore dollars` MINUS `the sum paid by the applicants, in Singapore dollars` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `the expenses of and incidental to the investigation, in Singapore dollars` MINUS `the sum paid by the company, in Singapore dollars` MINUS `the sum paid by the applicants, in Singapore dollars`   -- "any balance of the expenses not paid either by the company or the applicants"
    ELSE 0   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): there is no balance, so nothing is paid out of moneys provided by Parliament

§ `Section 238: the report as evidence`

-- src:22269 | 238. A copy of the report of any inspector appointed under this Part,
-- src:22270 | certified as correct by the Minister, is admissible in any legal
-- src:22271 | proceedings as evidence of the opinion of the inspector and of the
-- src:22272 | facts upon which the inspector’s opinion is based in relation to any
-- src:22273 | matter contained in the report.
@ref s 238 (src:22269-22273)
GIVEN `the copy is a copy of the report of an inspector appointed under Part 9` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy is certified as correct by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 238 the copy is admissible in any legal proceedings as evidence of the inspector's opinion and of the facts upon which the opinion is based` MEANS
    IF `the copy is a copy of the report of an inspector appointed under Part 9` AND `the copy is certified as correct by the Minister`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section makes admissible "A copy of the report of any inspector appointed under this Part, certified as correct by the Minister"; whether any other copy is admissible is for the law of evidence, outside the text

§ `Section 239: the inspector's helpers`

-- src:22277 | 239.—(1) An inspector of a declared company may employ such
-- src:22278 | persons as the inspector considers necessary and in writing authorise
-- src:22283 | any such person to do anything the inspector could himself or herself
-- src:22284 | do, except to examine on oath or affirmation.
@ref s 239(1) (src:22277-22284)
GIVEN `the person is an inspector of a declared company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(1) the inspector may employ the persons the inspector considers necessary` MEANS
    IF `the person is an inspector of a declared company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "An inspector of a declared company"

@ref s 239(1) (src:22277-22284)
GIVEN `the person is an inspector of a declared company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is one the inspector could himself or herself do` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is to examine on oath or affirmation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(1) the inspector may in writing authorise the employed person to do the thing` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person is an inspector of a declared company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "An inspector of a declared company"
    ELSE (IF `the thing is to examine on oath or affirmation`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to do anything the inspector could himself or herself do, except to examine on oath or affirmation"
          ELSE (IF `the authority is in writing` AND `the thing is one the inspector could himself or herself do`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE NOTHING))   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the inspector may "in writing authorise any such person to do anything the inspector could himself or herself do"; the subsection says nothing of an oral authority or of a thing the inspector could not do

-- src:22286 | (2) Any officer or agent of a corporation who —
-- src:22288 | (a) refuses or fails to produce any book or document to any
-- src:22289 | person who produces a written authority of an inspector
-- src:22290 | given pursuant to subsection (1); or
-- src:22292 | (b) refuses or fails to answer any question lawfully put to him
-- src:22293 | or her by any such person,
-- src:22295 | shall be liable to be dealt with in the same manner as is provided in
-- src:22296 | section 236(5) for refusing or failing to comply with the request of an
-- src:22297 | inspector.
@ref s 239(2) (src:22286-22297)
GIVEN `the person is an officer or agent of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has refused or failed to produce a book or document to a person who produces a written authority of an inspector given under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has refused or failed to answer a question lawfully put to the person by such a person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(2) the officer or agent is liable to be dealt with in the manner provided in section 236(5)` MEANS
    IF `the person is an officer or agent of a corporation` AND (`the person has refused or failed to produce a book or document to a person who produces a written authority of an inspector given under subsection (1)` OR `the person has refused or failed to answer a question lawfully put to the person by such a person`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection makes liable "Any officer or agent of a corporation who" refuses or fails in the two ways it names; it does not say that no other failure is dealt with so

§ `Section 240: the suspension of actions and proceedings by a declared company`

DECLARE `s 240(1) kind of action or proceeding` IS ONE OF
    `s 240(1)(a) an action or proceeding by the company upon or in respect of a contract, bill of exchange or promissory note`
    `s 240(1)(b) an action or proceeding by the holder or any other person in respect of a bill of exchange or promissory note dealt with by or to the company`
    `s 240(1) an action or proceeding of any other kind`

-- The window: "On and after the appointment of an inspector ... until the expiration of 3 months after the inspector has presented the inspector's final report to the Minister".
-- Until the final report is presented the window has no end.
-- src:22301 | 240.—(1) On and after the appointment of an inspector in respect of
-- src:22302 | any declared company until the expiration of 3 months after the
-- src:22303 | inspector has presented the inspector’s final report to the Minister, no
-- src:22304 | action or proceeding may without the consent of the Minister (which
@ref s 240(1) (src:22301-22304)
GIVEN `the day of the action or proceeding` IS A DATE
      `the date the inspector was appointed in respect of the declared company` IS A DATE
      `the date the inspector presented the final report to the Minister, if the inspector has` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 240(1) the day falls within the suspension` MEANS
        `the day of the action or proceeding` AT LEAST `the date the inspector was appointed in respect of the declared company`
    AND (CONSIDER `the date the inspector presented the final report to the Minister, if the inspector has`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
         WHEN JUST `the date of the final report` THEN `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the date of the final report` `the day of the action or proceeding` 3 Months)

-- The days the suspension lasts, for the prohibition below: from the appointment to the last day of the 3 months after the final report.
@ref s 240(1) (src:22301-22304)
GIVEN `the date the inspector was appointed in respect of the declared company` IS A DATE
      `the date the inspector presented the final report to the Minister` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 240(1) the number of days from the appointment to the end of 3 months after the final report` MEANS
    (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date the inspector presented the final report to the Minister` 3 Months) MINUS `the date the inspector was appointed in respect of the declared company`

-- src:22301 | 240.—(1) On and after the appointment of an inspector in respect of
-- src:22302 | any declared company until the expiration of 3 months after the
-- src:22303 | inspector has presented the inspector’s final report to the Minister, no
-- src:22304 | action or proceeding may without the consent of the Minister (which
-- src:22305 | may be given generally or in a particular case and which may be given
-- src:22306 | subject to such conditions and limitations as the Minister thinks fit)
-- src:22307 | be commenced or proceeded with in any Court —
-- src:22309 | (a) by the company upon or in respect of any contract, bill of
-- src:22310 | exchange or promissory note; or
-- src:22312 | (b) by the holder or any other person in respect of any bill of
-- src:22313 | exchange or promissory note made, drawn or accepted by
-- src:22314 | or issued, transferred, negotiated or endorsed by or to the
-- src:22315 | company unless the holder or other person —
-- src:22317 | (i) at the time of the negotiation, transfer, issue,
-- src:22318 | endorsement or delivery thereof to the holder or
-- src:22319 | other person gave therefor adequate pecuniary
-- src:22320 | consideration; and
-- src:22322 | (ii) was not at the time of the negotiation, transfer, issue,
-- src:22323 | endorsement or delivery thereof to the holder or
-- src:22324 | other person or at any time within 3 years before that
-- src:22325 | time a member, officer, agent or employee of the
-- src:22330 | company or the wife or husband of any member,
-- src:22331 | officer, agent or employee of the company.
@ref s 240(1) (src:22301-22331)
GIVEN `the corporation is a declared company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind of action or proceeding` IS A `s 240(1) kind of action or proceeding`
      `the day of the action or proceeding` IS A DATE
      `the date the inspector was appointed in respect of the declared company` IS A DATE
      `the date the inspector presented the final report to the Minister, if the inspector has` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the Minister has consented to the action or proceeding, generally or in the particular case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action or proceeding is within the conditions and limitations of the Minister's consent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder or other person gave adequate pecuniary consideration at the time of the negotiation, transfer, issue, endorsement or delivery to the holder or other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the negotiation, transfer, issue, endorsement or delivery to the holder or other person` IS A DATE
      `the last day, on or before that day, on which the holder or other person was a member, officer, agent or employee of the company, or the wife or husband of one, if ever` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240(1) the action or proceeding is barred without the consent of the Minister` MEANS
    IF NOT `the corporation is a declared company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the subsection speaks of "any declared company"; section 243(5) applies the provisions "with respect to the investigation of declared companies" to an investigation of ownership "with the necessary modifications", and whether that reaches this suspension the text does not say (fork F-K29)
    ELSE (IF NOT `s 240(1) the day falls within the suspension` `the day of the action or proceeding` `the date the inspector was appointed in respect of the declared company` `the date the inspector presented the final report to the Minister, if the inspector has`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the bar runs only "On and after the appointment ... until the expiration of 3 months after the inspector has presented the inspector's final report"
          ELSE (IF `the Minister has consented to the action or proceeding, generally or in the particular case` AND `the action or proceeding is within the conditions and limitations of the Minister's consent`
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the bar is "without the consent of the Minister (which may be given generally or in a particular case and which may be given subject to such conditions and limitations as the Minister thinks fit)"
                ELSE (CONSIDER `the kind of action or proceeding`
                      WHEN `s 240(1)(a) an action or proceeding by the company upon or in respect of a contract, bill of exchange or promissory note` THEN JUST TRUE
                      WHEN `s 240(1)(b) an action or proceeding by the holder or any other person in respect of a bill of exchange or promissory note dealt with by or to the company` THEN
                          (IF `the holder or other person gave adequate pecuniary consideration at the time of the negotiation, transfer, issue, endorsement or delivery to the holder or other person`
                              AND NOT (CONSIDER `the last day, on or before that day, on which the holder or other person was a member, officer, agent or employee of the company, or the wife or husband of one, if ever`
                                       WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
                                       WHEN JUST `the connection day` THEN (`the connection day` EQUALS `the day of the negotiation, transfer, issue, endorsement or delivery to the holder or other person`
                                                                            OR `period: the date is within a period before` `the connection day` `the day of the negotiation, transfer, issue, endorsement or delivery to the holder or other person` 3 Years))
                           THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the holder or other person — (i) ... gave therefor adequate pecuniary consideration; and (ii) was not at the time ... or at any time within 3 years before that time a member, officer, agent or employee of the company or the wife or husband of any member, officer, agent or employee": an "unless" met
                           ELSE JUST TRUE)
                      WHEN `s 240(1) an action or proceeding of any other kind` THEN JUST FALSE)))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): a closed list: the bar covers an action or proceeding "(a) by the company upon or in respect of any contract, bill of exchange or promissory note; or (b) by the holder or any other person in respect of any bill of exchange or promissory note" (fork F-K30)

-- The bar as a prohibition for as long as the suspension lasts (derived from the bar; fork F-K16):
-- SHANT ... WITHIN n sunsets at n, which is the number of days the suspension lasts, computed above from the appointment and the final report.
@ref s 240(1) (src:22301-22307)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
      `the number of days the suspension lasts` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 231 party` `s 231 act`
`s 240(1) a person must not commence or proceed with an action or proceeding in a Court without the consent of the Minister during the suspension` MEANS
    PARTY `s 231 a person` `the name of the person`
    SHANT `s 240(1) commence or proceed with an action or proceeding in a Court without the consent of the Minister`
    WITHIN `the number of days the suspension lasts`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 231 a person` `the name of the person` BECAUSE "the person commenced or proceeded with an action or proceeding in a Court without the consent of the Minister while it was suspended"

-- src:22333 | (2) Any action or proceeding which is commenced or proceeded
-- src:22334 | with in contravention of this section is void and of no effect.
@ref s 240(2) (src:22333-22334)
GIVEN `the action or proceeding was commenced or proceeded with in contravention of section 240` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240(2) the action or proceeding is void and of no effect` MEANS
    IF `the action or proceeding was commenced or proceeded with in contravention of section 240`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection makes void "Any action or proceeding which is commenced or proceeded with in contravention of this section"; whether any other action is void is outside it

§ `Section 241: winding up`

DECLARE `s 241(1) deemed applicant` IS ONE OF
    `s 241(1)(c) the company`
    `s 241(1)(d) a creditor or contributory of the foreign company upon the liquidation of the company in the place in which it is incorporated`

-- src:22338 | 241.—(1) An application to the Court —
-- src:22340 | (a) in the case of a company — for the winding up of the
-- src:22341 | company; or
-- src:22343 | (b) in the case of a foreign company — for the winding up so
-- src:22344 | far as the assets of the company in Singapore are concerned
-- src:22345 | of the affairs of the company,
-- src:22347 | may be made by the Minister at any time after a report has been made
-- src:22348 | in respect of a declared company by an inspector whereupon the
-- src:22349 | provisions of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution
-- src:22350 | Act 2018, with such adaptations as are necessary, apply as if —
-- src:22352 | (c) in the case of a company — a winding up application had
-- src:22353 | been duly made to the Court by the company; and
-- src:22355 | (d) in the case of a foreign company — an application for an
-- src:22356 | order for the affairs of the company so far as assets in
-- src:22357 | Singapore are concerned to be wound up in Singapore had
-- src:22358 | been duly made to the Court by a creditor or contributory
-- src:22359 | of the company upon the liquidation of the company in the
-- src:22360 | place in which it is incorporated.
-- src:22362 | [40/2018]
@ref s 241(1) (src:22338-22362)
GIVEN `a report has been made in respect of the declared company by an inspector` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241(1) the Minister may apply to the Court for the winding up` MEANS
    IF `a report has been made in respect of the declared company by an inspector`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the application "may be made by the Minister at any time after a report has been made in respect of a declared company by an inspector"; a "may" gated by "at any time after" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, items (b) and (c); fork F-K7)

@ref s 241(1) (src:22347-22360)
GIVEN `the Minister has applied to the Court after a report has been made in respect of the declared company by an inspector` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 241(1) deemed applicant`
`s 241(1) the application is treated as having been made by` MEANS
    IF `the Minister has applied to the Court after a report has been made in respect of the declared company by an inspector`
    THEN (IF `the body is a foreign company`
          THEN JUST `s 241(1)(d) a creditor or contributory of the foreign company upon the liquidation of the company in the place in which it is incorporated`
          ELSE JUST `s 241(1)(c) the company`)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 applies "as if" the application had been made, for an application "made by the Minister" under the subsection; an application by anyone else is not the subsection's

-- src:22364 | (2) Where, in the case of a foreign company, on any application
-- src:22365 | under subsection (1) an order is made for the affairs of the company
-- src:22366 | so far as assets in Singapore are concerned to be wound up in
-- src:22367 | Singapore the company must not carry on business or establish or
-- src:22368 | keep a place of business in Singapore.
@ref s 241(2) (src:22364-22368)
GIVEN `the body is a foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on an application under subsection (1) an order has been made for the affairs of the company so far as assets in Singapore are concerned to be wound up in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241(2) the foreign company must not carry on business or establish or keep a place of business in Singapore` MEANS
    IF `the body is a foreign company` AND `on an application under subsection (1) an order has been made for the affairs of the company so far as assets in Singapore are concerned to be wound up in Singapore`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the duty arises "Where, in the case of a foreign company, on any application under subsection (1) an order is made"; a "where" unmet on a duty (fork F-K5)

@ref s 241(2) (src:22364-22368)
GIVEN `the name of the foreign company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 231 party` `s 231 act`
`s 241(2) the foreign company must not carry on business or establish or keep a place of business in Singapore once the order is made` MEANS
    PARTY `s 231 a foreign company` `the name of the foreign company`
    SHANT `s 241(2) carry on business or establish or keep a place of business in Singapore`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 231 a foreign company` `the name of the foreign company` BECAUSE "the foreign company carried on business or established or kept a place of business in Singapore after the order to wind up its affairs there"

§ `Section 242: penalties`

-- src:22372 | 242.—(1) Any person who, with intent to defeat the purposes of
-- src:22373 | this Part or to delay or obstruct the carrying out of an investigation
-- src:22374 | under this Part —
-- src:22379 | (a) destroys, conceals or alters any book, document or record
-- src:22380 | of or relating to a declared company; or
-- src:22382 | (b) sends or attempts to send or conspires with any other
-- src:22383 | person to send out of Singapore any such book, document
-- src:22384 | or record or any property of any description belonging to or
-- src:22385 | in the disposition or under the control of such a company,
-- src:22387 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:22388 | not exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:22389 | 2 years.
@ref s 242(1) (src:22372-22389)
GIVEN `the person acted with intent to defeat the purposes of Part 9 or to delay or obstruct the carrying out of an investigation under Part 9` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person destroys, conceals or alters a book, document or record of or relating to a declared company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person sends or attempts to send, or conspires with another person to send, out of Singapore a book, document or record of a declared company or property of any description belonging to or in the disposition or under the control of a declared company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 242(1) the person is guilty of the offence of defeating the purposes of Part 9 or obstructing an investigation` MEANS
    IF `the person acted with intent to defeat the purposes of Part 9 or to delay or obstruct the carrying out of an investigation under Part 9` AND (`the person destroys, conceals or alters a book, document or record of or relating to a declared company` OR `the person sends or attempts to send, or conspires with another person to send, out of Singapore a book, document or record of a declared company or property of any description belonging to or in the disposition or under the control of a declared company`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): an element of the offence is unmet ("Any person who, with intent ... (a) destroys, conceals or alters ...; or (b) sends or attempts to send ... shall be guilty of an offence"); split site (i); fork F-K10

@ref s 242(1) (src:22372-22389)
GIVEN `the person acted with intent to defeat the purposes of Part 9 or to delay or obstruct the carrying out of an investigation under Part 9` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person destroys, conceals or alters a book, document or record of or relating to a declared company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person sends or attempts to send, or conspires with another person to send, out of Singapore a book, document or record of a declared company or property of any description belonging to or in the disposition or under the control of a declared company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 242(1) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `the person acted with intent to defeat the purposes of Part 9 or to delay or obstruct the carrying out of an investigation under Part 9` AND (`the person destroys, conceals or alters a book, document or record of or relating to a declared company` OR `the person sends or attempts to send, or conspires with another person to send, out of Singapore a book, document or record of a declared company or property of any description belonging to or in the disposition or under the control of a declared company`)
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 10000, 24, FALSE, FALSE)   -- "a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years": "or", so not both; no default penalty
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the penalty is fixed only for a person the subsection makes guilty

@ref s 242(1)(a) (src:22372-22389)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 231 party` `s 231 act`
`s 242(1)(a) a person must not destroy, conceal or alter a book, document or record of a declared company with intent to defeat the purposes of Part 9` MEANS   -- fork F-K34: a prohibition derived from the offence of s 242(1); the text names the bearer ("Any person who, with intent")
    PARTY `s 231 a person` `the name of the person`
    SHANT `s 242(1) destroy, conceal or alter a book, document or record of or relating to a declared company with intent to defeat the purposes of Part 9`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 231 a person` `the name of the person` BECAUSE "the person destroyed, concealed or altered a book, document or record of or relating to a declared company with intent to defeat the purposes of Part 9 or to delay or obstruct an investigation"

@ref s 242(1)(b) (src:22372-22389)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 231 party` `s 231 act`
`s 242(1)(b) a person must not send a book, document, record or property of a declared company out of Singapore with intent to defeat the purposes of Part 9` MEANS   -- fork F-K34: a prohibition derived from the offence of s 242(1); the text names the bearer ("Any person who, with intent")
    PARTY `s 231 a person` `the name of the person`
    SHANT `s 242(1) send out of Singapore a book, document, record or property of a declared company with intent to defeat the purposes of Part 9`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 231 a person` `the name of the person` BECAUSE "the person sent or attempted to send, or conspired to send, a book, document, record or property of a declared company out of Singapore with intent to defeat the purposes of Part 9 or to delay or obstruct an investigation"

-- src:22391 | (2) If in any prosecution for an offence under this section it is
-- src:22392 | proved that the person charged with the offence —
-- src:22394 | (a) has destroyed, concealed or altered any book, document or
-- src:22395 | record of or relating to the company; or
-- src:22397 | (b) has sent or attempted to send or conspired to send out of
-- src:22398 | Singapore any book, document or record or any property of
-- src:22399 | any description belonging to or in the disposition or under
-- src:22400 | the control of the company,
-- src:22402 | the onus of proving that in so doing the person had not acted with
-- src:22403 | intent to defeat the purposes of this Part or to delay or obstruct the
-- src:22404 | carrying out of an investigation under this Part shall lie on the person.
@ref s 242(2) (src:22391-22404)
GIVEN `it is proved in a prosecution for an offence under section 242 that the person charged did an act mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 242(2) the person bears the onus of proving that the person did not act with the intent` MEANS
    IF `it is proved in a prosecution for an offence under section 242 that the person charged did an act mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the onus lies on the person only "If in any prosecution for an offence under this section it is proved that" the person did the act; an "if" unmet (fork F-K5)
